              "text": "Because the word **\"doge\"** originated on the internet, its pronunciation was debated for years. However, a clear standard has emerged. \n\nThe official, dictionary-accepted pronunciation of **doge** is **\"DOHJ\"** (rhymes with \"vogue,\" but ends with a soft **\"j\"** sound like the beginning of *Jack* or *George*).\n\n### 1. The Standard Pronunciations (How to Say It)\nThere are two highly accepted ways to pronounce the word, and you can use either:\n* **\"DOHJ\"** (/do\u028ad\u0292/) \u2013 This is the most common pronunciation for the meme, the cryptocurrency (Dogecoin), and the historic rulers of Venice. It sounds like the word **\"dough\"** with a **\"j\"** at the end.\n* **\"DOHZH\"** (/do\u028a\u0292/) \u2013 Very similar to \"DOHJ,\" but it ends with a soft, French-sounding \"zh\" (like the \"g\" in *mirage* or *genre*, or the \"s\" in *measure*). \n\n### 2. Common (But Technically Incorrect) Alternatives\nBecause people first read the word online rather than hearing it spoken, several incorrect pronunciations became popular:\n* **\"DOHG\"** (rhymes with *vogue* or *rogue* with a hard \"g\").\n* **\"DODGE\"** (like the car brand or the game *dodgeball*). This is incorrect because \"doge\" uses a long \"o\" (doh), not a short \"o\" (dah).\n* **\"DOG-EE\"** (doggy) or **\"DOH-gay\"**. \n\n---\n\n### Why is it pronounced \"DOHJ\"? (The Origin)\nThe word actually has two entirely different histories, but both point to the same pronunciation:\n\n#### The Internet Meme Origin\nThe use of \"doge\" as a misspelling of \"dog\" dates back to a **2005** episode of the popular internet puppet show ***Homestar Runner***. In the episode, Homestar Runner refers to Strong Bad as his \"d-o-g-e,\" pronouncing it out loud as **\"dohj\"** (or \"dohzh\") to be intentionally silly. When the famous Shiba Inu meme went viral in 2013, internet users adopted the spelling and the cartoon's original pronunciation.\n\n#### The Historical Origin\nLong before the internet, a \"doge\" was the elected chief magistrate/ruler of the historic republics of Venice and Genoa (such as the famous *Doge's Palace* in Italy). In English, this historical title has always been pronounced **\"DOHJ\"**. (In Italian, it is pronounced *\"doh-jeh\"*).\n\n### Summary\nIf you are talking about the **Shiba Inu meme**, **Dogecoin**, or the US federal government advisory group (**D.O.G.E.**), the universally accepted way to say it is **\"DOHJ\"**.",
